cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TRIAD, please cite it with the data in this file."
title: "TRIAD: Trusted RDF Interoperable Agent Data"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Asish A.
    family-names: George
    affiliation: University of Victoria
  - given-names: Mohamed
    family-names: Khaled
    affiliation: University of Victoria
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohamedKhalidmk/TRIAD"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
version: 5.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
abstract: >-
  A data model for clinical records that many people make and change over time.
  Each clinical fact is an assertion with an author and a source, and a new assertion
  supersedes the old one, so the current state is the result of a traversal.
  The prototype is a hospital web app with a Care Assistant chat. Milestone 4 keeps the data in SQLite.
  Milestone 5 adds an OWL 2 ontology, a W3C R2RML mapping to an RDF knowledge graph in Virtuoso 7.2,
  SPARQL 1.1 scripts, and SPARQL adapters, so the same app runs on SQLite, Virtuoso or Oxigraph.
  The clinical entities follow HL7 FHIR R4. All data is synthetic (Synthea).
keywords:
  - clinical records
  - provenance
  - HL7 FHIR
  - relational database
  - SQLite
  - RDF
  - OWL
  - SPARQL
  - knowledge graph
  - Virtuoso
